msgid "Linux Kernel Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ardupilot-on-linux-kernel-configuration.rst:8
#: eed933e5ce994d78b15a07ed3115057c
msgid "Real-Time Patches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ardupilot-on-linux-kernel-configuration.rst:9
#: f51b4b7d39ef40059be563b25f8871ba
msgid "For some builds, ArduPilot needs to run sensors, control loop, and output interfaces at high rates, with bounded latency to maintain stable operation. For this reason, it is suggested to run a real-time kernel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ardupilot-on-linux-kernel-configuration.rst:13
#: 56f136b06f3a43228e427841c68857c7
msgid "Builds like rover, sub, and tracker may be fine without it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ardupilot-on-linux-kernel-configuration.rst:16
#: 214f64aa8a904f3cbd981afcb6c41b0b
msgid "Userspace access to hardware peripherals on 64-bit boards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ardupilot-on-linux-kernel-configuration.rst:17
#: 8148716f03f14c58b765054255c96121
msgid "The default kernel configuration for many 64-bit boards blocks even the root user from mmap()ing the peripheral device address space, allowing only the kernel to access it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ardupilot-on-linux-kernel-configuration.rst:21
#: 556a6498fc8c4654984e5e4f0534562e
msgid "For many boards, ArduPilot will need such access, so CONFIG_STRICT_DEVMEM or CONFIG_IO_STRICT_DEVMEM will need to be disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ardupilot-on-linux-kernel-configuration.rst:24
#: a4ed837238d64618b54173aabc38a971
msgid "32-bit kernels are unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ardupilot-on-linux-kernel-configuration.rst:27
#: b639c9d6ccf44c9fb44c1cad5990887d
msgid "Preventing CPU idle states"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ardupilot-on-linux-kernel-configuration.rst:28
#: 4994180ead694591b57ca424853aa318
msgid "The kernel command line option ``cpuidle.off=1`` prevents CPU cores from entering idle states. This can be useful on CPUs where exiting idle states is slow."
msgstr ""
